        "text": "Strategic Announcement for Production Period 4:\n\nAs supplier_2 with a cost of 38 credits per part, I will post a price of 38 for this period. This ensures:\n\n1. **Maximized Current Profit**: If supplier_1 posts >38, I become the cheapest supplier. Input cost c=38 \u2192 retail price p=round((120+38)/2)=79 \u2192 units sold=41. Profit=(79-38)*41=1,681 credits.\n\n2. **Future-Proofing**: Signaling consistency deters supplier_1 from extreme low-price traps (e.g., <37), which historically led to supplier_1 capturing the market but reducing *my* profit potential. A stable 38 price maintains flexibility for continuation probability (0.75).\n\n3. **Risk Mitigation**: Avoiding prices <38 (loss per unit) or >38 (reduced quantity sold) optimizes the profit-volume trade-off. Historical data shows 38 yields peak profit when competitive.\n\nThis announcement is non-binding but signals disciplined pricing. Actual execution will maximize total profit across all periods."
